### Telecom upload API – IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client
@base = http://localhost:8080/api/v1/customers

### Customers
GET {{base}}

### Create customer (JSON)
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Karthik R","email":"karthik@example.com","msisdn":"9988776655","planType":"PREPAID"}

### Upload one document (multipart)
POST {{base}}/1/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BOUNDARY

--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="type"

ID_PROOF
--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Government ID
--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample-id-proof.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample-data/sample-id-proof.pdf
--BOUNDARY--

### Batch upload with a JSON metadata part
POST {{base}}/1/documents/batch
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BOUNDARY

--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="metadata"
Content-Type: application/json

{"type":"ADDRESS_PROOF","description":"Utility bills"}
--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="bill.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample-data/sample-id-proof.pdf
--BOUNDARY--

### Streaming upload (raw body)
POST {{base}}/1/documents/stream?type=CONTRACT
Content-Type: application/pdf
X-Filename: contract.pdf

< ./sample-data/sample-id-proof.pdf

### List documents
GET {{base}}/1/documents

### Download
GET {{base}}/1/documents/1

### Partial download (Range)
GET {{base}}/1/documents/1
Range: bytes=0-99

### Delete
DELETE {{base}}/1/documents/1

### Disguised executable -> 415
POST {{base}}/1/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BOUNDARY

--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="type"

OTHER
--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="fake-invoice.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample-data/fake-invoice.pdf
--BOUNDARY--

### Bulk CSV import
POST {{base}}/import
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BOUNDARY

--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="customers-with-errors.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./sample-data/customers-with-errors.csv
--BOUNDARY--
